    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.base16\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nThe window separator character, displayed when `laststatus` is set to not show a status line everywhere, is hidden, because the `WinSeparator` and `VertSplit` highlight groups's foreground and background colors are both set to the same color (`base02`). This is in contrast to mini.hues's `randomhue` not having this issue.\r\n\r\nThe `VertSplit` highlight group should also not be used because it's deprecated.\r\n\r\nSetting `WinSeparator` to the background still doesn't look as good because of the different color of the number line on the left side.\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\n0.9.4\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n1. Use the mini.base16 module with any palette.\r\n2. Set the vim `laststatus` option to something like 3.\r\n3. Open another window in a split, like with `:split` or `:vsplit`.\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\nThe foreground and background colors of both the `WinSeparator` and `VertSplit` highlight groups should be different, so that the separator in between windows can be visible when using a `laststatus` option that hides the status line in some cases.\r\n\r\nThe `VertSplit` highlight group should also not be set at all, because it's deprecated according to Neovim's documentation (`:help hl-VertSplit`).\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\nInstead, the foreground and background colors of both the `WinSeparator` and `VertSplit` highlight groups are both set to `base02` (according to the source code of the plugin), which leads to the window separator character (default \"─\") being essentially invisible because both the foreground and background colors are the same.\r\n\r\nIn addition to that, the `VertSplit` highlight group shouldn't be set, as it's deprecated.\r\n\r\nI don't know if this is a bug or a feature; it could be that it's intended to hide the window separator to compensate for the supposed inconsistency of the number line on the left side being displayed with another background color. Here's what it looks like after setting `WinSeparator` to the background:\r\n![Here's what it looks like after setting `WinSeparator` to the background.](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/50467323/b72e17a4-34be-45cb-9742-32a2f4561c46)\r\nMaybe this issue can be avoided by disabling the coloration of the number line and instead having it just be the background (which I, myself, would prefer) or by having this fix/feature available as a configurable option. Setting the `LineNr*` highlight groups to the background looks like this:\r\n![Setting the `LineNr*` highlight groups to the background looks like this:](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/50467323/9c463537-5d0e-4850-a2d1-1c6300f50f5b)",
