        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\nI am aware of this issue and agree with you that it doesn't look as good as 'mini.hues' and your second example (with gutter and window separators having same background as `Normal`). However, 'mini.base16' is set to follow Base16 standard, which [has it this way](https://github.com/chriskempson/base16-vim/blob/3be3cd82cd31acfcab9a41bad853d9c68d30478d/templates/default.mustache#L230).\r\n\r\nIf any reasonable deviation to be made, it makes sense to have it patch other issues. Like adjusting `FloatBorder` to have the same background color as window itself, etc. I am not yet sure how I feel about making this deviation.\r\n\r\nDropping \"VertSplit\" is reasonable, but not an issue in itself (as it just one extra highlight group which is not used). It is there to, again, have more in common with 'base16-vim'.\r\n\r\nI'll let this be open for a while and think about it.",
