        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "I guess that would make sense considering the author of that Vim plugin also created Base16 and the Tomorrow themes. The official, albeit somewhat vague, [Base16 style guide](https://github.com/chriskempson/base16/blob/main/styling.md) also does suggests base16-vim as a reference, but not necessarily as a strict set of guidelines.\r\n\r\nHowever there are also other Base16 (Neo)vim plugins like [this one](https://github.com/RRethy/nvim-base16/tree/master) that seem to be more popular (but unofficial) and implement things in a slightly differently way.",
